//! The `text-decoration-skip` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets
//! what parts of an element's content any text decoration affecting the element must skip over. It
//! controls all text decoration lines drawn by the element and also any text decoration lines drawn
//! by its ancestors.
//!
//! Initial: objects. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: Nothing is skipped. Thus, text decoration is drawn for all text content and across atomic
//! inline-level boxes.
//!
//! Grammar: none | auto
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-4/#propdef-text-decoration-skip
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-decoration-skip
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

module std.css.properties.TextDecorationSkip.

